function renderValidationFuture(){
 return pageHeader('Validation','Future workstream · architecture reserved now, operational implementation later.')+`<div class="future-workstream-banner"><span class="status neutral">FUTURE MODULE</span><div><h2>One validation thread from requirement to verified evidence</h2><p>DV, PV, engineering validation, reliability and customer-specific programmes will use the same products, DUTs, people, equipment, methods, quality records and planning engine already established by Prototype.</p></div></div>${futureWorkstreamFlow(['Requirements','Validation plan','Test legs / DUTs','Constrained plan','Execute','Results','Verify requirements'])}<div class="grid cols-2 future-workstream-grid"><div class="card"><span class="eyebrow">TEST DEVELOPMENT</span><h2>Missing method becomes controlled development</h2><p>A validation requirement that cannot use a released standard method will create a development activity, with estimate, resources, qualification/commissioning evidence and formal release into the shared Test Library.</p>${futureWorkstreamFlow(['Method gap','Develop','Qualify','Release','Reuse'])}</div><div class="card"><span class="eyebrow">SHARED BACKBONE</span><h2>No duplicate validation database</h2><p>Product/configuration, build/DUT genealogy, specifications, methods, equipment/calibration, competency, measurements, quality cases, approvals, documents and audit history remain shared canonical objects.</p></div></div><div class="callout"><strong>POC boundary:</strong> this menu entry intentionally reserves the product architecture without creating pretend validation records or disconnected functionality.</div>`;
}
function renderFailureAnalysisFuture(){
 return pageHeader('Failure Analysis','Future workstream · connected investigation and verification, not a separate ticket database.')+`<div class="future-workstream-banner"><span class="status neutral">FUTURE MODULE</span><div><h2>Trace a failure back through the complete engineering record</h2><p>Failures may originate from prototype build, validation, incoming inspection, production/field evidence or a manual investigation request. The case will remain linked to the exact DUT, build/configuration, process revision, equipment state and test evidence where known.</p></div></div>${futureWorkstreamFlow(['Failure intake','Triage / contain','Evidence','Hypotheses','Analysis / experiments','Root cause','Corrective action','Verify / retest','Learn'])}<div class="grid cols-2 future-workstream-grid"><div class="card"><span class="eyebrow">CONNECTED EVIDENCE</span><h2>Investigation starts with context already known</h2><p>DUT genealogy, material lots, process parameters, route revisions, calibration certificates, operators, measurements, deviations and validation results can become evidence without re-keying them into another system.</p></div><div class="card"><span class="eyebrow">CLOSED LOOP</span><h2>Correction must prove effectiveness</h2><p>A corrective action can require a rebuild, a validation retest or both. Closure happens only after verification evidence is linked; recurrence can reopen the learning loop.</p></div></div><div class="callout"><strong>POC boundary:</strong> the framework is visible now so Prototype is built on the eventual LabOS operating model. Full FA workflow remains a future implementation.</div>`;
}
